;; packages module — the merged package-system counter.
;;
;; the merged one keeps what the former packages_* modules each
;; hardcoded: the entry's :args lists candidate backends, tried in
;; order — (packages :args ["pacman"]) — and the first hit wins as
;; "N (backend)"; no :args means the full list in the same order, so a
;; bare (packages) entry reads the machine it runs on. the list is
;; per-target: the linux backends (apk, dpkg, emerge, eopkg, pacman,
;; pkgtool, xbps) hold only on the linux build, and the BSD targets
;; carry their own one-level /var/db/pkg counter — so a foreign
;; directory never masquerades as another package system's database.
;;
;; the preset takes the list as one named argument, so the lip declares
;; :arg :args — the cross-check keeps the param named in module.zig
;; and the entry's list spelling in config.lip.
(module
    :fn "preset"
    :deps [:io]
    :arg :args)
